      "seed": 1264552022,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 695293933,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793600000000,
      "created": 1793600000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Jobs\n- PK job_id\n- user_id, task_id, schedule, parameters\n- GSI user_id\n\nExecutions\n- PK time_bucket#shard  (hour + hash(job_id) % N)\n- SK execution_time#job_id\n- status: PENDING | QUEUED | RUNNING | SUCCEEDED | FAILED\n- attempt, user_id, task_id, parameters\n\nExecution query table\n- PK user_id#k\n- SK execution_time",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Jobs\n- PK job_id\n- user_id, task_id, schedule, parameters\n- GSI user_id\n\nExecutions\n- PK time_bucket#shard  (hour + hash(job_id) % N)\n- SK execution_time#job_id\n- status: PENDING | QUEUED | RUNNING | SUCCEEDED | FAILED\n- attempt, user_id, task_id, parameters\n\nExecution query table\n- PK user_id#k\n- SK execution_time",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "cwHgq1oi85Un5CfM6dh9Z",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 900,
      "width": 814.0000000000001,
      "height": 525.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "al",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 915415628,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1473383155,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793600000000,
      "created": 1793600000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Deep dive\n\n1. How to execute jobs within 2s of the scheduled time?\n- two layers: DB for durability, delay queue for precision\n- Watcher scans the next 5 min every 5 min, send(delay = exec_time - now)\n- Service Bus scheduled message / SQS DelaySeconds (<= 15 min)\n- a new job due within the current window -> enqueue directly\n\n2. How to scale to 10k/s?\n- Executions PK time_bucket#shard, Watchers own shards by lease\n- status query off the hot path: change feed -> query table\n- workers: AKS + KEDA, min replicas, pre-scale by upcoming count\n\n3. How to ensure at-least-once?\n- visibility timeout / peek-lock, heartbeat renew, retry with backoff, DLQ\n- idempotent by execution_id, conditional write with epoch (fencing)\n- reconciler re-enqueues stuck executions\n\n4. Recurring jobs?\n- keep only the next execution, create the next one on enqueue / complete\n- compute in the user's time zone, store in UTC",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Deep dive\n\n1. How to execute jobs within 2s of the scheduled time?\n- two layers: DB for durability, delay queue for precision\n- Watcher scans the next 5 min every 5 min, send(delay = exec_time - now)\n- Service Bus scheduled message / SQS DelaySeconds (<= 15 min)\n- a new job due within the current window -> enqueue directly\n\n2. How to scale to 10k/s?\n- Executions PK time_bucket#shard, Watchers own shards by lease\n- status query off the hot path: change feed -> query table\n- workers: AKS + KEDA, min replicas, pre-scale by upcoming count\n\n3. How to ensure at-least-once?\n- visibility timeout / peek-lock, heartbeat renew, retry with backoff, DLQ\n- idempotent by execution_id, conditional write with epoch (fencing)\n- reconciler re-enqueues stuck executions\n\n4. Recurring jobs?\n- keep only the next execution, create the next one on enqueue / complete\n- compute in the user's time zone, store in UTC",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
